From 54934964aaa1dd80476a4c173c23522906d1f809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:23:54 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Provide arc4random() and its companions where glibc has none

glibc has had arc4random(), arc4random_uniform() and arc4random_buf()
only since 2.36 (2022).  Code written for Apple's C library or a BSD's
calls them freely, and on an older glibc, such as Ubuntu 22.04's 2.35
(the oldest LTS still supported, which AppImages are built on so they
run on older systems), it builds with an implicit declaration and then
fails to link.

On such a glibc the base library now declares them (GSArc4Random.h,
imported by NSObjCRuntime.h, so with Foundation) and provides them in
Source/Additions/GSArc4Random.c: bytes from getrandom(), or /dev/urandom
on a kernel without it, and arc4random_uniform() without modulo bias.
On any other C library, glibc 2.36 and later among them, the header
declares nothing and the file compiles to nothing.

The test calls the three functions through Foundation: on glibc 2.35 it
fails to link without this change and passes with it.
---
 Headers/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.h |   1 +
 Headers/GNUstepBase/GSArc4Random.h |  51 +++++++++++++
 Source/Additions/GNUmakefile       |   1 +
 Source/Additions/GSArc4Random.c    | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 Source/GNUmakefile                 |   1 +
 Tests/base/Functions/arc4random.m  |  67 +++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 235 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Headers/GNUstepBase/GSArc4Random.h
 create mode 100644 Source/Additions/GSArc4Random.c
 create mode 100644 Tests/base/Functions/arc4random.m

